B15. Teach an elderly person about cybersecurity topic of your choice.

In this activity, I taught my grandad about the topic of threat intelligence during a family online call since I am not currently with any family member at Perth.
I explained how threat intelligence transforms scattered cyber data into 'intelligence' to counter extortion and scams by hackers. To make it easy, I simply broke down complex cyberattack into four core:
adversary, capability, infrastructure and victim.
I used a concept of burglar like their break in tools, escape routes and the vimtimized household which successfully helping him to understand how hackers exploit vulnerabilities to steal senitive information.
We also discussed 'Pyramid of Pain' concept, to show him why simply changing password or blacking IPs is easy for thieves to bypass and how truly causes pain to the hackers by disrupting their tactics with tools as the top of the Pyramid.
Finally, I shown him the importance of the role of 'feedback' thath reporting suspicious texts or phishing mails in real time as the most effective defensive action.
